  "html": "<div><section><div><section><p>This is the currently published alpha baseline and remains subject to final professional legal review.</p><div><blockquote><strong>INTERIM PUBLIC ALPHA BASELINE.</strong> This policy defines the current authorized reporting channel and testing boundaries.</blockquote><p><strong>Effective date:</strong> August 17, 2026<br><strong>Last updated:</strong> November 3, 2026<br><strong>Contact:</strong> <a href=\"mailto:security@tenvor.io\">security@tenvor.io</a></p><p>Tenvor welcomes good-faith reports that help protect customers, compute providers, and the Service. This policy describes how to report a suspected vulnerability. It does not authorize testing outside the boundaries below.</p><h2 id=\"in-scope\">In scope</h2><ul><li>tenvor.io and explicitly identified Tenvor-owned API hosts;</li><li>the current public Tenvor worker/node release;</li><li>authentication, authorization, API-key, account-separation, job-recovery, billing-integrity, settlement, payout, sandbox, protocol-signature, and privacy issues; and</li><li>accidental exposure of credentials or Customer Content.</li></ul><h2 id=\"out-of-scope-without-written-permission\">Out of scope without written permission</h2><ul><li>denial of service, load testing, resource exhaustion, or actions affecting availability;</li><li>accessing, modifying, retaining, or downloading another person’s data beyond the minimum proof necessary;</li><li>social engineering, phishing, physical intrusion, or attacks on personnel or operators;</li><li>testing Clerk, Cloudflare, hosting, payment, GitHub, model, or other third-party systems;</li><li>automated scanning that generates high traffic or account creation;</li><li>economic manipulation;</li><li>public disclosure before Tenvor has had a reasonable opportunity to investigate and remediate; and</li><li>any activity prohibited by law.</li></ul><h2 id=\"good-faith-rules\">Good-faith rules</h2><ul><li>Use your own account, keys, node, and data.</li><li>Stop immediately if you encounter Customer Content, personal data, credentials, or a path to economic loss.</li><li>Do not exploit beyond the minimum needed to demonstrate impact.</li><li>Do not retain or share exposed data.</li><li>Do not demand payment or threaten disclosure.</li><li>Preserve timestamps, release versions, request IDs, and non-sensitive reproduction steps.</li></ul><h2 id=\"how-to-report\">How to report</h2><p>Email <a href=\"mailto:security@tenvor.io\">security@tenvor.io</a> with:</p><ul><li>affected host, release, endpoint, or component;</li><li>vulnerability type and impact;</li><li>safe reproduction steps;</li><li>relevant request/job IDs without prompt content;</li><li>whether any data or account may be exposed;</li><li>your preferred contact and disclosure timeline; and</li><li>a request for an encrypted channel before sending secrets or sensitive evidence.</li></ul><p>Do not send private keys, raw API keys, illegal content, or another user’s Customer Content by ordinary email.</p><h2 id=\"tenvor-s-response\">Tenvor’s response</h2><p>Tenvor aims to acknowledge a report within <code>five business days</code>, provide a status update within <code>30 days</code>, and coordinate remediation and disclosure based on severity. These are response targets, not a service-level agreement.</p><p>Tenvor may ask for clarification, a safe retest, or identity information needed for a reward or legal requirement. Tenvor does not promise a bounty. Any reward is discretionary unless a separate published program says otherwise.</p><h2 id=\"safe-harbor-statement\">Safe-harbor statement</h2><p>Where you comply with this policy, act in good faith, avoid privacy/economic harm, and promptly report the issue, Tenvor will not initiate legal action against you for the authorized research. If a third party initiates action and you complied with this policy, Tenvor may confirm that your activity was conducted under the policy.</p><p>This safe harbor applies only to claims Tenvor has authority to release. It does not bind law enforcement, regulators, customers, compute providers, or third parties and does not authorize violation of law.</p></div></section></div></section></div>"
